{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1450980-manage-a-gunfight","id":1450980,"title":"Manage a gunfight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-04T13:49:30-07:00","id":1450980,"title":"Manage a gunfight","content":"If a garou take the wrong decision and become the target of 3 or 4 shooters, and they would shoot him all at the same time how would you go to roll their action? 1 by 1 for their to-hit roll and damage roll or mix their dice roll to solve it in a single roll? Like take the higher dice pool of the shooters and add one dice per additional shooters maybe? I'm trying to reduce the number of roll during a fight to prevent my player from getting bored, including classic &quot;to-hit, to-defense, damage, soaking&quot; rolls, there's tto much roll in a single action for us","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 06-04-2021, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T09:09:30-07:00","id":1451333,"title":"","content":"It depends on how deadly you want the combat to be. If the weapons are high powered (and especially if they have silver ammunition) this can be a real danger to the players. Rules as written have you roll it out for each shooter. I agree this is too much so I do one of the following based on how challenging the fight needs to be.<br /> <br /> * A significant challenging (shows that Garou are still mortal): Before the session, roll the attack and base damage for each shooter for your estimated number of rounds (I default to 3). Add or subtract based on the soak roll made in-games by the player. This still involves a roll on your part but not multiple rolls.<br /> <br /> * A minor challenge (shows off how tough Garou can be): Assume all shooters have the same weapon and stats and make one attack roll before the session. Use that for each antagonist during the session.<br /> <br /> In both cases I subtract anything that gives the character defense (such as cover, dodging, and certain Gifts) directly from the successes rolled rather than re-rolling. If this completely nerfs the attack than so be it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, it looks like you prefer a less granular system than the rules as written. One thing I do is use the same initiative for all standard or low-level antagonists, and use one attack roll for all of them using the same type of weapon. For unique or high-powered antagonists I handle each one like a PC and just deal with the slow pace. Your suggestion to make one roll and add dice for each attacker is interesting. Mechanical analysis is not my strong suit but some of the other posters are probably much better suited to address that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T08:08:23-07:00","id":1451666,"title":"","content":"The problem with so much roll when there's a fight is that for me and my friends it may take more than one game of 3 hours to solve 30 minutes of in-game action, that's why i'm looking for some tricks to speed up the game, your system is interesting, if a group of soldier roll their attack one time in the beggining and it's a fail or a botch you re-roll it next and all the stats are already set up, the rest is up to the player <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> In my case to reduce the number of roll i'm working on a new mechanic, to apply full damage in certain situation, apply full soak for certain type of attack (for exemple never full soak on fire, poison, radiation and other damages that afflict a character for multiple round):<br /> <br /> For exemple, when 2 character attack each other in the same time with a gun or claws or anything, the one who touch is the one with more success, and since its enemy do not try to defend by dodging or blocking, he take full damage but with his full soak if he can absorb lethal or aggravated damages (like a spiral dancer or a strong fomori)<br /> <br /> When we try to defend ourselves by dodging, blocking or anything, our character initiate a movement which avoid him to take a full punch, so we roll the damage to know how much the attack touch and apply full soaking (that rule work for a failed defense roll, if the defense is a botch the character react to late and take full damages)<br /> <br /> Before you say that a character, garou or other, with full soaking would be invulnerable, i've set up a rule to ignore a part of the soaking when you target a specific area of the body (eyes, throat, articulation, not protected zone in the case of an armor etc..) and in addition, every additionnal success on the attack roll are auto damage and not just damages dices to roll with the rest of the pool.<br /> <br /> My system is not complete yet but I'm working on it and testing it with a character sheet that I'm modifying to evaluate several character types on several situations, and I am quite satisfied of the result for now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 06-11-2021, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}